d_line_warnings in the Gradle documentation.\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 13m\n9 actionable tasks: 1 executed, 8 up-to-date\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791378696793}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_trHbK16uIhOvGDWnENNGk8oO|fc_0f3ffc0c6dbb400e016ac64507427887d1974d199b14d38706", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Research complete. I compared this request against the existing, much richer test suites for the *same* library's later versions (11.0.18/11.0.22/11.0.23) already in this repo — these already solved an equivalent coverage-expansion problem for tomcat-embed-core, so they're strong precedent for what setup is actually needed.\n\n**Key findings:**\n- The 11.0.x suites cover JNDIRealm, JAASRealm, DefaultInstanceManager, JDBCAccessLogValve, DataSourceLinkFactory, WebdavServlet, and ~15 other Catalina subsystems that 10.0.20's current single-class `TomcatTests.java` never touches — these are exactly the kind of `typeReached`-gated JMX/reflection paths the shipped metadata encodes, so exercising them is what would move the needle on the 528-call gap.\n- None of that richer suite needs Docker or a real external service: `JNDIRealmTest` mocks SSL hostname verification instead of hitting a real LDAP server, `JAASRealmTest` uses a local `.config` resource file, and `JDBCAccessLogValveTest`/`DataSourceLinkFactoryTest` use an **in-memory H2** JDBC URL (`jdbc:h2:mem:...`) or a hand-rolled `RecordingDataSource` — never a container.\n- Two test dependencies not in 10.0.20's current `build.gradle` are present in those richer suites: `com.h2database:h2:2.2.224` and `jakarta.annotation:jakarta.annotation-api:3.0.0` (needed for `DefaultInstanceManager`'s `@Resource`/`@PostConstruct`/`@PreDestroy` reflective injection path).\n- Those suites also add JVM args (`--add-opens` for several JDK modules, a Digester system property, and `-Djava.home=...` for native-test runtime) to exercise JRE-compat and classloader-leak-prevention classes — these are test-code/runtime setup, not deterministic Maven/Docker setup.\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nThis repo's own metadata/tests directories across versions act as a natural experiment log: when a coverage effort already succeeded for a newer version of the identical artifact, its `build.gradle` diff *is* the ground truth for what infra was actually required — far more reliable than guessing from documentation, since it already passed this repo's native-image verification gate.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"Broadening coverage requires exercising Realm/Valve/naming subsystems (JNDIRealm, JAASRealm, DefaultInstanceManager, JDBCAccessLogValve, DataSourceLinkFactory, etc.) that the current single TomcatTests.java never reaches. The sibling 11.0.18/11.0.22/11.0.23 test suites for this same library already did this and needed two extra testImplementation dependencies, but no Docker image or external service - JNDI/JAAS/JDBC realms are all exercised with in-memory/mocked substitutes.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"com.h2database:h2:2.2.224\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"In-memory JDBC driver used by JDBCAccessLogValve/DataSource-backed naming-resource tests (jdbc:h2:mem: URL) - no container needed. Version matches what's already proven for this library's 11.0.18/11.0.22/11.0.23 suites.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"jakarta.annotation:jakarta.annotation-api:3.0.0\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"Supplies @Resource/@PostConstruct/@PreDestroy types needed to drive DefaultInstanceManager's annotation-based reflective injection path. Same coordinate used across this library's newer sibling test suites.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"No Docker image or real directory/LDAP/database server is required: JNDIRealm tests mock SSL hostname verification rather than contacting a real LDAP server, JAASRealm tests use a local tomcat/jaas-realm-resource.config test resource, and JDBC-backed tests use an in-memory H2 URL. If tests are added that exercise JreCompat/classloader-leak-prevention/digester-system-property paths (mirroring JreCompatTest, JreMemoryLeakPreventionListenerTest, DigesterTest in the 11.0.x suites), add these JVM args to the javaTest task: --add-opens=java.base/java.io=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.lang=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.lang.reflect=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.util=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.rmi/sun.rmi.transport=ALL-UNNAMED, and the system property -Dorg.apache.tomcat.util.digester.PROPERTY_SOURCE=org.apache.tomcat.util.digester.SystemPropertySource. Only add the specific flags a given new test actually needs rather than copying all of them speculatively. If any such test runs under nativeTest, also set runtime arg -Djava.home=<JAVA_HOME or GRAALVM_HOME>.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"jakarta.annotation-api 3.0.0 targets Jakarta EE 11 while 10.0.20 otherwise pins jakarta.servlet-api 5.0.0 (EE9); it's additive and compiles fine (confirmed by the 11.0.x precedent), but a stricter EE-generation match would be 2.0.0/2.1.1 if that's preferred.\",\n    \"Precedent is based on later Tomcat versions (11.0.x); confirm via local checkMetadataFiles/test runs that the same Realm/Valve/naming classes are structurally unchanged in 10.0.20 before relying on it, since local Gradle and Native Image verification remain authoritative.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791378696794}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_IP4LO18IHlIGMNEAzUvXEpyH|fc_0f3ffc0c6dbb400e016ac64507428087d1aa24b0507d8025f8", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Prompt:\nYou are preparing a Forge workflow for a library issue. Decide whether the library needs setup beyond the normal generated test scaffold before meaningful coverage is reachable.\n\nResearch the library yourself to make this decision. Investigate the resolved artifact and its dependencies, how the library is normally used, and its documentation. The JSON context below is only a starting point, not the limit of what you may consider. Do not modify the repository or apply any setup yourself — return only the decision. Local Gradle and Native Image verification remain authoritative.\n\nThe setup can be one of three things: an extra Maven dependency, a Docker image the tests need, or an environment/system property the generated tests must set. Represent dependencies and Docker images as `deterministic_setup` entries the driver can apply before generation:\n  - {\"kind\": \"dependency\", \"coordinate\": \"group:artifact:version\", \"scope\": \"testImplementation\", \"reason\": \"...\"}\n  - {\"kind\": \"docker_image\", \"image\": \"name:tag\", \"slug\": \"short-slug\", \"reason\": \"...\"}\nIf a test needs a Docker image that is already pinned under `tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/`, reuse the exact tag from that `Dockerfile-<slug>` instead of introducing a new one, since the allow-list permits a single shared tag per image.\nPut environment variables, system properties, and other test-code setup in `agent_guidance`. Do not restate deterministic entries as guidance.\n\nReturn a single JSON object with this shape:\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\" | \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"short reason\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [ ... dependency or docker_image entries, if any ... ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"environment/system property/test setup guidance, if any\",\n  \"risks\": [\"risk notes, if any\"]\n}\n\nChoose no_action unless your research finds concrete evidence that extra setup is needed.\n\nContext (starting point):\n{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 10508,\n    \"title\": \"Improve coverage for org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.0.20\",\n    \"label\": \"library-update-request\",\n    \"body\": \"### Reason for requesting the library\\n\\nWe want to increase dynamic access coverage. The tests for `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.0.20` currently cover 55 of 528 recorded dynamic access calls (10.4%). This version was added before the dynamic access coverage process existed, so its tests never exercised most of the reflective and resource accesses the shipped metadata declares. The request is to extend the tests so they drive those accesses.\",\n    \"body_error\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"library\": \"org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.0.20\",\n  \"current_library\": null,\n  \"new_version\": null,\n  \"existing_tests\": {\n    \"org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.0.20\": [\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/.gitignore\",\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/build.gradle\",\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/gradle.properties\",\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/settings.gradle\",\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/user-code-filter.json\",\n      \"tests/src/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/10.0.20/src/test/java/tomcat/TomcatTests.java\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nConversation:\n{\"duration_api_ms\":214250,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"a0f5be4a-102f-4bbe-ae70-0d679ca2f4e7\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.5937068000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":22,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":66080,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":758264,\"output_tokens\":17769,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":11899},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":66080,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":5574,\"cache_read_inpu