tion-api 3.0.0 targets Jakarta EE 11 while 10.0.20 otherwise pins jakarta.servlet-api 5.0.0 (EE9); it's additive and compiles fine (confirmed by the 11.0.x precedent), but a stricter EE-generation match would be 2.0.0/2.1.1 if that's preferred.\\\",\\n    \\\"Precedent is based on later Tomcat versions (11.0.x); confirm via local checkMetadataFiles/test runs that the same Realm/Valve/naming classes are structurally unchanged in 10.0.20 before relying on it, since local Gradle and Native Image verification remain authoritative.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"ttft_ms\":5216,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":227980,\"uuid\":\"ae48c18e-0f33-46c2-a61c-d3db5a1e8a57\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2288,\"time_to_request_ms\":600,\"first_content_frame_ms\":2292,\"queued_turn_count\":0,\"result_index\":0}\n\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791378696795}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_uKkGFsREFwPInOIIw1hrtrUc|fc_0f3ffc0c6dbb400e016ac64507428c87d1bfcde6ab5dd2e01a", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "> Task :tck-build-logic:extractPluginRequests UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:generatePluginAdapters UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileJava UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovy UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovyPlugins UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:pluginDescriptors UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:processResources UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:classes UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:jar UP-TO-DATE\n\n> Configure project :\nGraalVM Reachability Metadata TCK\n---------------------------------\n\n> Task :populateArtifactURLs\nI've confirmed the current state of the `10.0.20` entry in the file. Here's what I found:\n\n**All five content fields are already non-blank:**\n- `source-code-url`, `repository-url`, `test-code-url`, `documentation-url`, `description` — all populated.\n- `language` — absent (not present as a key at all).\n\nPer the instructions, I may only fill fields that are **missing** (absent/null/blank) and must leave already-populated fields untouched. The only candidate here is `language`.\n\n**Is tomcat-embed-core language-specific?** No. It's the embedded Tomcat servlet container core, written in plain Java with no Kotlin/Groovy/Scala binding or dependency. The spec is explicit: \"Set missing 'language' only when the library is language-specific; otherwise leave the field absent.\" Since it isn't language-specific, the correct value is to leave it absent — which is exactly its current state.\n\n**Conclusion: no edit is needed.** The entry already satisfies every requirement in the task (correct non-blank URLs/description, and `language` correctly absent for a non-language-specific library), so I'm not modifying the file.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThis task template is shared across many metadata entries in bulk automation (used for both \"fill in missing field\" runs and \"URL maintenance\" runs). The two instruction blocks you saw — one about filling only missing fields, another about treating existing URLs as templates to re-verify \"when URL maintenance is requested\" — are conditionally relevant depending on which mode triggered the task. Nothing in this invocation said URL maintenance was being requested, so the unconditional \"do not modify non-blank fields\" rule governs, and the pre-filled URLs (Maven Central sources jar, GitHub repo root, GitHub tree paths for test/docs) are left as-is even though I could independently confirm they look reasonable for Tomcat's versioning scheme.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\nRan agent for org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.0.20 (exit 0). Log: /home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10508-4a05b067/build/agent-url-discovery-logs/org.apache.tomcat.embed-tomcat-embed-core-10.0.20.log\nCompleted populateArtifactURLs: invoked=1, prompted=0, skipped=0, overwriteExisting=false, verifyArtifactSources=fal