olCallId": "call_Zv4rQFgPa1POb9PtydsP4w7v|fc_0aae1c8da5179779016ac62dfdd7cc87d1a99ed4c8828d2890", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"continueFrom\": \"explore\",\n  \"coordinate\": \"org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1\",\n  \"failure\": {\n    \"operand\": \"reporter-requested metadata\",\n    \"phase\": \"explore\",\n    \"step\": \"generate_tests()\"\n  },\n  \"issueNumber\": 9730,\n  \"label\": \"library-new-request\",\n  \"libraryPreparationPreflight\": {\n    \"action\": \"no_action\",\n    \"agent_guidance\": \"This artifact only ships org.springframework.boot.micrometer.metrics.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMetrics and MetricsContextCustomizerFactory (+ nested DisableMetricsExportContextCustomizer). Without @AutoConfigureMetrics on a @SpringBootTest class, the customizer forces metrics export off for that test context; with it present, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration/MetricsAutoConfiguration/SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration/ObservationAutoConfiguration are auto-imported so a MeterRegistry (e.g. SimpleMeterRegistry) is actually registered. A meaningful test pair is: (1) a minimal @SpringBootTest WITHOUT the annotation asserting no usable MeterRegistry bean / metrics export is suppressed, and (2) one WITH @AutoConfigureMetrics asserting a MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) \\u2014 this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.\",\n    \"applied_setup\": [],\n    \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n    \"input_evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"issue\",\n        \"summary\": \"#9730 Support for org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1; label=library-new-request; body_chars=39\"\n      },\n      {\n    