 MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) \\\\u2014 this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.\\\",\\n    \\\"applied_setup\\\": [],\\n    \\\"deterministic_setup\\\": [],\\n    \\\"input_evidence\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"issue\\\",\\n        \\\"summary\\\": \\\"#9730 Support for org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1; label=library-new-request; body_chars=39\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"existing_tests\\\",\\n        \\\"summary\\\": \\\"0 existing test file path(s) included\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"input_tokens_used\\\": 32,\\n    \\\"issue_label\\\": \\\"library-new-request\\\",\\n    \\\"issue_number\\\": 9730,\\n    \\\"library\\\": \\\"org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"sonnet\\\",\\n    \\\"output_tokens_used\\\": 14707,\\n    \\\"risks\\\": [\\n      \\\"This is the first 'real' artifact in the spring-boot-*-test family to be onboarded here \\\\u2014 its sibling POM-only starters (e.g. spring-boot-starter-micrometer-metrics-test) are already marked not-for-native-image with this artifact as the replacement, but there's no prior PR in this repo for a sibling like spring-boot-webmvc-test/spring-boot-restclient-test to cross-check the exact test shape against.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n    \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Pure test-support SPI module (one annotation + one ContextCustomizerFactory, registered via bundled META-INF/spring.factories). All classes it activates (MetricsAutoConfiguration, SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration, ObservationAutoConfiguration) are already transitive compile dependencies 